  "records": {
    "description": "32 bit sequential divider. Takes in two numbers A (max. 32 bit) and B (max. 31 bit) and computes A // B, i.e. the integer part of A divided by B. For example, dividing 7 by 2 returns 3. It uses non-restoring division, so B can only be 31 bit at most.",
    "input": "two numbers A (max. 32 bit) and B (max. 31 bit)",
    "output": "A // B, i.e. the integer part of A divided by B",
    "speed": "It takes 32 cycles on a 11t clock, so 11t * 32 = 352t = 35.2 seconds, no matter what the inputs are.",
    "considerations": [
      "The remainder can technically be recovered as well, but sometimes one would have to perform an additional restoring step at the end, so do another addition, but I didnt see a nice way to do this."
    ]
  },
